  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strenghtening the Cross-Border Cooperation and Border Management Capacities of North Macedonia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is to contribute to the efforts of the Government of the Republic of North Macedonia to strengthen border management capabilities in addressing cross-border crime, including smuggling of migrants and trafficking in human beings, in line with international standards and with a human right- and gender-based approach. To achieve the project objective, IOM will work towards the achievement of the following two outcomes: 1) National Border Police from the country&#x2019;s Southern border demonstrates an increased cross-border cooperation capacity with the Border Police of Greece in addressing cross-border crime, including smuggling of migrants and cases of violence, exploitation, abuse in full respect of the rule of law and human rights; and 2) Strengthened technical border management capabilities leads to improved border surveillance.</narrative>
  </description>
